# Only code and a few summary figures are tracked. Everything else in this
# folder (about 65 GB of single-cell and bulk data, intermediate results and
# old versions) stays on the local disk. README.md says how to get the data.
#
# How the rules work: ignore every file, keep looking inside folders,
# re-include code files, then shut out folders that hold data or old versions.

# Ignore every file ...
*
# ... but keep looking inside folders, so the rules below can re-include files.
!*/

# Code and docs
!*.py
!*.R
!*.r
!*.Rmd
!*.Rproj
!*.sh
!*.ipynb
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/README_PIPELINE.md
!/requirements.txt
# summary figures shown in README.md
!/figures/*.png

# Data, results and old versions: never tracked, even where they contain code
/GSE*/*/
/TCGA_Data/*/
/Metabric/*/
/MET500/*/
/PRIMARY/*/
/PRIMARY_OLD_backup/
/composite/
/JSHS_submission/
/common/cache/
/ARCHIVE/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
